# STRESS 03 — HAIRLINES
#
# A weight ramp from 0.1pt to 3pt, with the value printed beside every stroke.
# Print it and find the first weight your printer renders at its declared
# thickness rather than at one device pixel — everything below that line is a
# property of the printer, not of the document.
#
# TWO THINGS THIS SHEET WILL TEACH YOU ABOUT THE TOOL ITSELF:
#
#   * Every stroke is floored at 0.25pt (geom.TicksPerPt/4). The 0.1pt, 0.15pt
#     and 0.2pt rows are therefore drawn at 0.25pt and are identical to it. The
#     floor is silent — there is no diagnostic — so the three rows looking the
#     same is correct behaviour, not a rasterisation artefact.
#   * Horizontal and vertical strokes of the same weight rasterise differently
#     on most laser printers, so both are on the sheet.

page
  size: letter
  margin: 0.5in

defaults
  font: IBM Plex Mono
  font-size: 8pt
  color: gray(0.12)

section
  height: 26pt
  text "03 · HAIRLINES"
    font-size: 15pt
    font-weight: bold
    tracking: 1.2pt

section
  height: 26pt
  text "Left column gray(0), right column gray(0.6). The first three rows are below the 0.25pt floor and are drawn at 0.25pt."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

